  "id": "jump-arc",
  "name": "JumpArc",
  "kind": "struct",
  "declaration": "public struct JumpArc: Sendable, Equatable",
  "abstract": "A ballistic parabola in window space.",
  "discussion": [
   "For air progress u ∈ [0,1]:\n  x(u) = start.x + (end.x − start.x)·u\n  y(u) = lerp(start.y,end.y,u) − 4·peakHeight·u·(1−u)",
   "`peakHeight` is the EXTRA peak above the straight start→end chord (the\n4·u·(1−u) term is 0 at both ends and 1 at u=0.5), so a same-level jump\npeaks exactly `peakHeight` points above the perch."
  ],
  "availability": [],
  "conforms": [
   "Sendable",
   "Equatable"
  ],
